          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The commit check is complaining that you have not selected the \"Allow commits from members who can merge to the target branch\" option in your merge request.\n\nTo find this setting, look in the top-right corner of the merge request page for a button named \"Edit\", and select that button.  Scroll all the way to the bottom of the edit page, and the checkbox you seek should be directly above the \"Save changes\" button.  Ensure that the checkbox is checked, and choose \"Save changes\".  That will hopefully allow the commit check to succeed.\n\n(There is currently an entirely separate problem with the formatting of error messages reported by the commit check, which is why the error messages are a bit mangled... we're working on fixing that display issue now.)",
